Whisper: show why Whisper's download check held a file

What: lets a verdict string of Whisper's own download check ("WhisperHeld:<reason>")
through DownloadCore unchanged; the downloads panel and about:downloads show Whisper's
title and reason for it (WhisperDownloadGuard.describe) and offer "Allow download" and
"Remove file" as for an uncommon file; the confirmation when allowing it does not call
the file malware.
Why: the check itself plugs into Firefox's Integration overrides (no patch), but
Firefox maps every verdict it does not know to "" and its views throw on an unknown
verdict, so without these lines a held file would show no reason at all and could
not be allowed.
---
diff --git a/browser/components/downloads/DownloadsCommon.sys.mjs b/browser/components/downloads/DownloadsCommon.sys.mjs
--- a/browser/components/downloads/DownloadsCommon.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/downloads/DownloadsCommon.sys.mjs
